# Build context for backend.Dockerfile. BuildKit reads
# <dockerfile>.dockerignore in preference to a context-root .dockerignore,
# which is what keeps every Docker file inside docker/ without dropping an
# ignore file into the project root.
#
# The context is the project root (doctor_Assistant/), so paths below are
# relative to that.

# Everything, then re-admit only what the backend image needs. Safer than an
# exclusion list: a new secret file added to the project is out by default.
*

!backend/
!docker/entrypoint.sh

# --- carved back out of backend/ -------------------------------------------

# Secrets and per-machine configuration. The container is configured entirely
# through environment variables (APP_ENV=production makes config.py look for
# config/prod.ini, which does not exist, so nothing falls back to a file).
backend/.env
backend/config/dev.ini
backend/config/prod.ini

# Local virtualenv, ~200 MB and Windows-built -- useless in a Linux image.
backend/venv/

# The Windows ffmpeg.exe copy. The image installs Debian's ffmpeg instead.
backend/.bin/

# Runtime state that belongs in a volume, not an image layer.
backend/uploads/
backend/logs/
backend/*.log

# Caches and editor droppings.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
backend/.pytest_cache/
backend/migrations/
